c_ms = t_s+t_d-t_f (t_f from off baseline). c/t_d is the scaling ratio (thesis: ~flat).
ART_auto = engine runtime value (parsed from log; b//2 if never updated).
ART_deriv = b*(c/t_d), the value the adaptive formula prescribes.
breakdown ms = mean per occurrence from --ee_profile sidecar (data: kvfill,bufstg; control: upd_kv,stepsync,skipmask; resid = c - sum, the two-pass/launch fixed cost).
c_ms is from the rebatch cell; breakdown ms are from the separate prof cell (different invocation -> expect noise).
Breakdown is an attribution (CPU-launch timers + optional sync), not an exact partition.

